WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:06.150
<i>I started a Duel with the Charlie, owner of Number 7, the card with the strongest luck!</i>

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:09.820
<i>Plus the location is a rampaged monorail which has lost control.</i>

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.070
<i>If this continues, we'll...</i>

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.620
Mayumi-<i>chan</i>.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.210
It’s almost time for your surgery.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:25.960
Yeah...

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.500
Don’t worry, it will be over while you're still asleep.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.380
Yeah...

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.590
But my uncle still hasn't...

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:37.550
Yuma…

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.230
Alright, Yuma. Let our Carnival begin!

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:48.980
Gotcha, here I come! My turn, draw!

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:55.360
I'll set a Monster in face-down Defense Position! And set one more card, ending my turn!

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:58.910
<i>Is he really planning to win with luck alone?</i>

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:01.580
My turn, draw!

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.330
I activate the Continuous Magic, Trading Game!

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.960
Let's start out small. Let me test my luck a bit!

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:15.300
This card allows me to toss a die once per turn, and if I tossed a six, my current Life will increase five times!

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:20.850
However, if I get another value, my Life will return to the value prior to activation!

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.850
As if you'll get a six that easily!

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:35.400
No. He managed to roll five consecutive sixes in the previous Duel. The odds of the next one being 6 is 1/46656.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.320
Behold…

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.450
It’s definitely impossible!

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:39.820
There!

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.210
S-Six?! He got it again?!

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:50.250
Five times 4000 is 20000!

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.300
So long as the sun is round, my luck won't end!

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.100
Shut up! The sun set a long time ago, darn it!

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.010
Right, which means nothing can stop my fortune.

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:07.730
I Summon Majestic Jester!

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:15.070
I attack the Monster in face-down Defense Position with Majestic Jester!

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:18.280
He attacked with a zero Attack Power Monster?!

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.240
Desperate Mime!!

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:31.710
Gogogo Golem’s DEF is 1500. You're the one who’s taking damage!

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:36.420
What a pity, Yuma. I activate the effect of Majestic Jester!

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.420
<i>More</i> dice?!

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.640
Allow me to utilize this extraordinary luck to its fullest!

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:47.020
When Majestic Jester declares an attack, if I tossed a six, it destroys a Monster my opponent controls.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:50.440
If I got other values, then this card is destroyed and says his goodbye.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:56.780
The probability of another consecutive six is 1/129936.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.360
L-Like heck he will!

00:02:58.360 --> 00:02:59.530
Here I come!

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:00.740
Here!

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.580
It can't be!

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:11.750
Impossible!

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:15.880
Bingo! I destroy Gogogo Golem!

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.800
I set one card, and end my turn!

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:31.350
If this continues, we will…

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:37.070
Fret not! We're standing next to the world's luckiest good luck charm, after all!

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.220
<i>As I get closer, I stretch my hand out</i>

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:44.270
<i>towards that shining light leading towards tomorrow</i>

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:51.530
<i>I dream of a world that expands from my feet.</i>

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:00.790
<i>I haven't a clue of where things like dreams and hopes are at.</i>

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:05.290
<i>Even if I run looking for it, I still can't seem to find it.</i>

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:11.750
<i>I wonder if I have fallen into a gap of truth and lies.</i>

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:16.550
<i>Even so, our grand tale has yet to begin.</i>

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:22.220
<i>Let's move on towards tomorrow, 
even if our road begins to fall apart.</i>

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:27.480
<i>I will jump forward, before all my
 strength completely drains.</i>

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.360
<i>The closer I get, the further it becomes,</i>

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:33.650
<i>that truth that I must seize.</i>

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:38.820
<i>It's to find hope that we desire from a future unseen.</i>

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.410
<i>With a heart stronger than anyone else,</i>

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.580
<i>I'll learn to keep running up.</i>

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:50.130
<i>With the strength to win any battle, 
despite just how weak I am,</i>

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:52.630
<i>My purpose is to find,</i>

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:55.630
<i>with these invaluable friends of mine,</i>

00:04:55.630 --> 00:05:02.430
<i>The future of the world expanding
 from my feet with my own eyes.</i>

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.580
Charlie...! Charlie!

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:22.460
He completely disappeared after that, and no one knew where he went. That idiot!

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:24.670
"Number 32: The Insurmountable Luck!
 Number 7, Lucky Stripes!"

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.590
My turn, draw!

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:30.140
I Summon Gagaga Magician!

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:36.020
In that case, I'll win with luck as well!

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:39.150
I activate Magic Card, Monster Slot!

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:49.410
I Banish one Monster in my Graveyard who has same level as Gagaga Magician!

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:58.670
And I card allows me to draw one card from my deck, if the drawn Monster has same level as those 2 Monsters, I can special summon it to my field!

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:05.420
But if it doesn’t match, the drawn Monster and targeted card will be Banished!

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:06.880
You're taking too many risks!

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.260
You are so annoying!

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:12.100
If I get it, I'll have enough materials for a Rank 4 Xyz Summon!

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:17.560
It seems you still don’t understand. I already absorbed your luck, so there's nothing left for you to use!

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:21.230
Gimme a break! C'mon, my good fortune!

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:21.900
Draw!

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.240
No way~!

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:35.370
I already told you! You can't surpass my luck!

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.910
Darn! I end my turn!

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:43.590
If this continues, our chances of defeating him will trickle down to zero percent...

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:46.960
Say what?! What the heck are you going on about?!

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:48.590
Don't you get it, Yuma?

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:51.930
The luck attached to my cards is absolute.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:07:00.100
Your father, Kazuma-<i>san</i>, was once my idol who greatly inspired me. I used to think he has everything.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:04.900
But there was one thing he lacked, and that was luck.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:05.570
What?

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:08.820
If only he had slightly better luck...

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.780
It had nothing to do with luck!

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:15.620
There are some critical moments in a person's life where they can't afford to lose.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:20.000
That’s right, even it means they have to win by relying on luck!

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:24.960
Here I come! My turn, draw!

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:30.420
Alright, here goes! The Continuous Magic, Trade Game! If I hit the jack pot, my Life will increase 5 fold!

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:36.760
It won’t come again!

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:41.140
A-Again?!

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:42.480
He rolled a six!

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:47.650
Life is Carnival! Now my Life is 100000!!!

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:52.610
100000 Life?? How can we ever beat that Life?

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:55.870
I activate the Magic Card, Release Change!

00:07:55.870 --> 00:08:01.500
By releasing one Monster on my field, I can Special Summon one Monster with the same level!

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:07.000
I release the Level One Majestic Jester, and Special Summon Diceslot Seven with the same level!

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:12.840
Then I activate the Magic Card, Monster Slot!

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.600
Damn! It's the same as me!

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:19.560
That’s right. What will happen if I do it?

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:23.890
I target the Level One Diceslot Seven!

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:29.360
I remove the Level One Majestic Jester from my Graveyard!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:38.780
Now, if I draw a Level One Monster, I can Special Summon that Monster!

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:47.880
Alright, here it comes! I Special Summon Diceslot Seven!

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.590
You gotta be kidding me!

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:55.970
Next, I Normal Summon the third Diceslot Seven!

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:02.390
We're in trouble, Yuma!

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:09.650
Diceslot Seven can raise its level according tot the tossed value until the End Phase!

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:12.400
Please, give me three sixes!

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:22.870
The odds of getting three sixes is 1/362790000!

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:25.080
Stop it! I don’t want to hear that!

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.370
Let’s finish this once and for all!

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.050
There it is!

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.670
Something so unreal... actually happened.

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:38.930
The level of all three Diceslot Sevens goes from one to seven!

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:44.680
I Overlay the three Level Seven Diceslot Sevens!

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:51.650
I build the Overlay Network with the three Monsters!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:54.440
Xyz Summon!

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:59.450
Come forth! Number 7! Lucky Stripe!

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:04.580
There it is!

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:05.620
The Number!

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:08.330
It's here, here, here, here!

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.960
LIFE IS CARNIVAL!

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.960
Darn it!

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:19.510
As I said, as long as the sun remains as one, whole unit...

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.310
...my good fortune won’t end!

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:32.190
Kotori-<i>chan</i>!

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:33.480
Akari-<i>san</i>?

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:40.160
Listen carefully, there's only five minutes left before this monorail reaches its destination.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:41.820
That means...

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:44.910
Don't worry, I'll handle it somehow.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:49.960
Yuma! We're close to the destination!

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:50.670
What?!

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:52.290
Here I come, Yuma!

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:55.050
I activate Lucky Stripe’s effect!

00:10:55.050 --> 00:11:00.720
When this Monster battles, by detaching one Overlay Unit, I roll a die!

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:08.430
And after the battle concludes, Lucky Stripe's Attack Power will increase by its original Attack Power times the number rolled on the die.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:14.440
Alright, here I go!

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:30.410
It’s six! Lucky Stripe’s original Attack Power is 700, so times six, it’s 4200!

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.830
4200?!

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:35.880
I attack you directly with Lucky Stripe!

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:37.250
Super Lucky Nova!!

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:38.800
Yuma, use the Trap!

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:39.720
Understood!

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:42.550
Trap Card, open! Clever Scheme!

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:48.020
When I'm about to receive a direct attack, by sending one Monster Card from my hand to the Graveyard,

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:51.770
this card reduces the Battle Damage equal to the Attack of the sent Monster!

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.810
I send Zubaba Knight to the Graveyard!

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:01.110
Yuma!

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.950
Oh, a Trap Card? Impressive indeed!

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:09.290
I end my turn.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.000
Damn it!

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.710
Hey, can't you do anything?!

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:17.380
If his fortune really is flawless, then there really is nothing we can do about it.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:18.710
You can’t be serious…

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.590
Hey! Yuma! What are you sulking about?

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.260
Sis!

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.550
Akari?

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:28.720
Charlie! Just you wait! I will get there to give you a good beating!

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:33.440
You're as passionate as ever! If it's a kiss you're after, I'd be glad to oblige!

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:39.320
Yuma, I guess you were crushed by Lucky Stripe, the card Charlie stole, Right?

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:42.860
I need to tell you something regarding that card!

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:48.080
When the sun splits in two, its power will be carried away with the wind.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:50.290
Huh? What's that supposed to mean?

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:53.750
It's a rumor that talks about how to take the luck away from that card.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.170
Take the luck away?

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:57.460
That's what I've been saying!

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:58.840
Life is Carnival!

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:03.220
It means my luck won't disappear as long as the sun is round and whole!

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.180
Two suns...?

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:08.680
And that's what makes this card's fortune absolute!

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.140
We don’t have much time left!

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:20.400
C'mon, Yuma. It's probably about the right time for you to be surrendering.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:25.900
As if! I... I'll never give up!

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:28.160
My turn! Draw!

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:30.660
I Summon Ganbara Knight!

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:38.500
When a Level Four Monster is Summoned successfully, I can Special summon Shadow Lizard from my hand!

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:45.630
All right, I overlay the Level Four Shadow Lizard and Ganbara Knight!

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:49.760
I build the Overlay Network with these two Monsters!

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.560
Xyz Summon!

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:55.310
Come forth, Number 39!

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:57.140
Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:01.520
I use Aspiring Emperor - Hope to attack Lucky Seven!

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:05.650
Permanent Trap, activate! Dice Crisis!

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:12.790
By tossing a die, if I get a six, this card makes the Attack Power of one Monster my opponent controls zero! I then gain control of it!

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:15.290
Ole!

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.750
It won’t show up!

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:19.500
Please, don’t show up!

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:27.930
Sorry to disappoint. I got a six again!

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:32.810
Now Hope belongs to me!

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:34.180
Hope…

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:38.480
I set one card and end my turn.

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:44.900
We're pretty close to the final stop.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:50.860
Allow me to finish to this Duel. After all, you can’t win anyway. Everything is fruitless in front of my strong luck!

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:54.700
You're pissing me off with this “luck, luck” talk!!

00:14:54.700 --> 00:15:00.170
It doesn't matter whether you have luck or not! All that matters is that a person tries their best in a fight! That's how Dueling should be!

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.790
Just like my Dad taught me!

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.460
Yuma…

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:11.180
My Dad never relied on luck! He always opened the path with his own strength! And I'll do the same!

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:14.220
Yuma…

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:17.180
I will not give up!

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:24.360
I get it. Then allow mew to finish this once and for all. My turn!

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:25.320
Yuma!

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:26.020
Right!

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:29.070
Hold on! Trap Card, open!

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:30.700
Command of Sword!

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:36.830
When there is a Light-Attribute Warrior-Type Monster on my side of field, I can activate this effect in my opponent’s Draw Phase!

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:39.750
Now draw your card!

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:49.510
If the drawn card is a magic or trap, I can either destroy the drawn card, or destroy one Magic or Trap card on the field.

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:55.220
Is that’s so? Your goal is to destroy Dice Crisis, and get Hope back!

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:56.850
Draw it, Charlie!

00:15:59.270 --> 00:15:59.930
Draw!

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:04.060
The card I drew is Sun’s Scale!

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:11.900
By tossing a die once per turn, if I get a six, all Monsters on my opponent’s field will be destroyed.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:18.410
Even you get back your Hope, my victory won’t change! As long as the sun is still round!

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.040
The sun...!

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:23.290
I target Dice Crisis…

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:24.920
Yuma, the sun!

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:27.210
Split the sun!

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:28.130
The sun?

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:31.840
As long as the sun is round and whole...?

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:34.300
I get it! So you mean...!

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:37.550
I can’t believe such thing could happen in a Duel!

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:41.930
According to the effect of Command of Sword, the selected warrior, Hope!

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:46.270
Cut the sun from the Magic Card, the Scale of Sun!

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:47.770
I-It can't be...!

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:52.110
Go, Hope!

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:55.450
Hope Sword Slash!!

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:07.080
The sun... became two!

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:18.930
That light is...

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:22.100
Don’t tell me the card’s power…

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:24.730
How could that happen?!

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:29.230
Because Scale of Sun was destroyed, you will receive 500 points of damage!

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:34.190
How can my luck disappear?!

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:36.700
I activate the effect of Trade Game!

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:42.040
If I roll a six, my Life will increase 5 fold! Otherwise it will return to its original value.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.040
One?!

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:59.640
So my fortune... really did vanish?

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.220
I end my turn...

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:02.680
Yuma, do it now!

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:06.730
Alright, my turn, draw!

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:11.020
I activate the Magic Card, Come Back!

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:15.570
It will recover one of my Monsters on my opponent’s field!

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:19.740
Come back, my Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:24.200
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!!

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.620
Chaos Xyz Change!

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:31.290
Now show your self, Chaos Numbers 39!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:39.340
The messenger who used the power of Hope to turn chaos into light! Aspiring Emperor - Hope Ray!

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:43.100
Aspiring Emperor - Hope Ray…

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:46.020
I activate the effect of Aspiring Emperor - Hope Ray!

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:51.480
By detaching one Overlay Unit, it gains 500 Attack Points!

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:53.610
Overlay Charge!

00:18:56.280 --> 00:19:02.200
And for every Overlay Unit detached, the opponent’s Monster’s Attack Power will decrease by 1000!

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:07.540
Go! I attack Lucky Stripe with Aspiring Emperor - Hope Ray!

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:10.210
Hope Sword Chaos Slash!!

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:27.890
Alright, I win!

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:28.730
Yuma!

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:29.940
The final stop!

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:32.770
We can’t make it!

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:39.650
Sis!

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:46.370
Akari's gonna bring it to ya!!

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:03.720
Sis!

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:05.800
Are two of you all right?

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:06.430
Yup!

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:07.010
Yes!

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:09.390
Thank goodness.

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:11.730
Right, where’s Charlie?

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:17.440
My luck… My luck has disappeared…

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:19.570
I'm so sorry, Mayumi...

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:20.530
Who's that?!

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:23.070
A..Akari!

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:26.410
Who's this woman named Mayumi?

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:31.370
Mayumi!

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.920
Uncle!

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:37.420
Sorry I'm late!

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:41.760
I brought those magic words with me! "Bring it to 'em", Mayumi!

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:43.300
Bring it to 'em?

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:45.010
Yeah, do your best!

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:45.800
Okay!

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:53.020
Plus, I will give this card to you as your lucky charm.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:58.150
Thanks! I'll bring it to 'em and do my best!

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:01.940
The card...

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:05.570
Maybe its luck came back when it changed ownership!

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:12.660
It’s going to be alright, the surgery will definitely be a success.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:17.880
I heard that girl's surgery comes with great difficulty.

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:22.550
So I... wanted to give my luck to her... along with that card.

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:24.220
Charlie…

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:28.010
- Even so, there was no need to do something like-
 - Akari!

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:35.230
Please tell Yuma for me that, "You're a splendid successor to Kazuma-<i>san</i>'s spirit of bringin' it to 'em."

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:36.310
That, and...

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:39.860
Thanks for your help, Akari.

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:46.030
Ouch, that hurt.

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:52.120
See you later! I hope you can dress a bit more casual the next time we meet.

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:57.290
Okay! The day's finally over!

00:21:57.290 --> 00:21:59.170
Yup! I'm hungry now!

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:02.210
Will she really return the Number to us?

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:03.840
It'll be fine!

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:08.720
No, I think we need to be more concerned about this! Hey! Yuma!

00:22:19.980 --> 00:22:23.150
<i>Someone gave me some water.</i>

00:22:23.530 --> 00:22:29.070
<i>So I was able to paint a rainbow with ease.</i>

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:35.000
<i>I want to become someone perfect.</i>

00:22:35.790 --> 00:22:38.040
<i>But it's very difficult.</i>

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:41.630
<i>Even with me suffering,</i>

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:45.710
<i>I can't seem to grasp victory.</i>

00:22:46.590 --> 00:22:48.550
<i>I want to bloom!</i>

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:52.970
<i>I must be having some kind of weird dream.</i>

00:22:52.970 --> 00:22:56.020
<i>But If I must fulfill this,</i>

00:22:56.520 --> 00:22:59.310
<i>Then I don't mind being laughed at for it.</i>

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:06.400
<i>Since it's because your limits are decided on your own.</i>

00:23:06.690 --> 00:23:09.450
<i>I'll show it, overcoming it to tomorrow.</i>

00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:13.950
<i>Ah, I'm aiming for the big blue sky.</i>

00:23:14.120 --> 00:23:15.870
<i>For all of its glory.</i>

00:23:15.870 --> 00:23:17.660
<i>The Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:23.040
<i>All of those countless flower petals</i>

00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:26.090
<i>They came at the expense of</i>

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:29.670
<i>me being able to reach those heights.</i>

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:34.100
<i>Ah, even though I lost my way today,</i>

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:35.930
<i>I still yearn for it.</i>

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:38.220
<i>That Freesia of Desire.</i>
